-- title:
--   Idèle boxes lie in the image of the idelic norm
-- statement:
--   Let $E$ and $F$ be number fields with $F$ a Galois extension of $E$, and let $B$ be an adele base-change datum from $\mathcal{O}_E, E$ to $\mathcal{O}_F, F$: a ring homomorphism $\beta$ from the adele ring of $E$ to that of $F$ commuting with the structure maps from $E$ and $F$, together with an isomorphism of $\mathbb{A}_E$-algebras $\mathbb{A}_E \otimes_E F \cong \mathbb{A}_F$ carrying $1 \otimes f$ to the image of $f$. Let $n$ be a natural number divisible by $[F:E]$, let $S$ be a finite set of height-one primes of $\mathcal{O}_E$, and let $H_v$ be a subgroup of $(E_v)^\times$ for each height-one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_E$ and $H_w$ a subgroup of $(E_w)^\times$ for each infinite place $w$ of $E$. Assume: (i) for every $v \in S$, either $H_v$ is contained in the image of the $n$-th power endomorphism of $(E_v)^\times$, or some prime $w$ of $\mathcal{O}_F$ lying over $v$ satisfies $\operatorname{finrank}_{E_v} F_w = 1$; (ii) for every $v \notin S$ and every prime $w$ of $\mathcal{O}_F$ over $v$, the inertia subgroup of $w$ in $\operatorname{Gal}(F/E)$ is trivial; (iii) for every infinite place $w$ of $E$ that is not unramified in $F$, $H_w$ is contained in the $n$-th powers of $(E_w)^\times$. Then the idèle box attached to $(S, (H_v), (H_w))$ — the subgroup of $\mathbb{A}_E^\times$ of those units whose finite part has $v$-component in $H_v$ for $v \in S$ and has both its $v$-component and the $v$-component of its inverse in the local integers for $v \notin S$, and whose component at each infinite place $w$ lies in $H_w$ — is contained in the range of the idelic norm of $B$, i.e. of the map on unit groups induced by the algebra norm of $\mathbb{A}_F$ over $\mathbb{A}_E$ taken along $\beta$.
--
--   This is the norm-side inclusion in Chevalley's algebraic proof of the second inequality of class field theory: a suitably small box of local conditions is shown to consist of idelic norms from $F$. It is used to prove openness of the image of the idelic norm and feeds the second-inequality statements for cyclic extensions generated by roots of unity.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_M4aHerbrand_AdeleBaseChange_ideleBox_le_range_idelicNorm.lean

